WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.780 --> 00:00:04.740
When the first trailer for the ninth Fast
and Furious film dropped at the Fast 9 Festival

00:00:04.740 --> 00:00:10.059
in Miami on January 31, fans of the nearly
two-decade-long action franchise were gifted

00:00:10.060 --> 00:00:11.580
a shocking surprise.

00:00:11.780 --> 00:00:16.860
After winning over audiences in 2006's The
Fast and The Furious: Tokyo Drift, Han Lue,

00:00:16.860 --> 00:00:21.220
the effortlessly cool street racer, thief,
businessman, and former member of Dominic

00:00:21.220 --> 00:00:23.380
Toretto's crew, is back from the dead.

00:00:23.740 --> 00:00:28.280
Played by Sung Kang, he died in the third
Fast and Furious movie, the first in the franchise

00:00:28.280 --> 00:00:29.740
directed by Justin Lin.

00:00:30.230 --> 00:00:33.820
Though he appeared in the next three films,
the saga's timeline puts his death after the

00:00:33.820 --> 00:00:35.720
events of Fast &amp; Furious 6.

00:00:35.960 --> 00:00:40.780
Thus, fans have believed for more than a decade
that Han's fate in the universe had been sealed.

00:00:40.980 --> 00:00:42.880
"Time for you to do your own thing."

00:00:47.560 --> 00:00:49.620
"Heard they're doing some crazy s--- in Tokyo."

00:00:49.900 --> 00:00:54.440
Yet, there he is in the trailer, characteristically
snacking as he enters a room full of his former

00:00:54.440 --> 00:00:55.340
crew mates.

00:00:55.440 --> 00:01:00.220
This, of course, begs the question: How is
Han still alive after audiences saw him die?

00:01:00.380 --> 00:01:02.540
We Got This Covered claims to know the answer.

00:01:02.660 --> 00:01:06.680
Take the following with a grain of salt, but
the outlet alleges that Han simply escaped

00:01:06.680 --> 00:01:09.220
his car before it became enveloped in flames.

00:01:09.500 --> 00:01:13.800
Unidentified and unverified sources close
to the outlet say that Han has been in hiding,

00:01:13.800 --> 00:01:17.980
staying under the radar of those he knows
would be after him following the fateful incident.

00:01:18.340 --> 00:01:21.720
The site also reported that the character
will make an appearance in the saga's 10th

00:01:21.720 --> 00:01:25.200
and final film, slated for an April 2021 release.

00:01:25.549 --> 00:01:30.140
However Han Lue makes his long-desired return
in F9, the news of his survival has been a

00:01:30.140 --> 00:01:33.200
shot of adrenaline to the fanbase of the Fast
franchise.

00:01:33.420 --> 00:01:37.120
After being with each other for more than
a decade, the cast has evolved into a family

00:01:37.120 --> 00:01:38.580
as much as the characters have.

00:01:38.760 --> 00:01:42.760
Han was a huge part of that, which helped
convince director Justin Lin to bring the

00:01:42.760 --> 00:01:45.780
character back into Dom's family and back
into the Fast universe.

00:01:45.960 --> 00:01:47.440
As Lin told Entertainment Weekly:

00:01:47.640 --> 00:01:50.920
"I think it's really up to us to bring him
back and explore it throughout the themes

00:01:50.920 --> 00:01:52.140
that we're all used to."

00:01:52.260 --> 00:01:53.860
The fans certainly seem happy.

00:01:54.000 --> 00:01:58.200
On Twitter, the announcement that Han would
return got the hashtag #HanIsAlive trending.

00:01:58.380 --> 00:02:02.859
It also appeared to renew the trust of Fast
diehards who felt betrayed by the movies after

00:02:02.859 --> 00:02:07.390
it gave Han's killer Deckard Shaw prime billing
in two films following the popular character's

00:02:07.390 --> 00:02:07.880
death.

00:02:07.940 --> 00:02:12.120
As it happens, Lin has a long history with
Han, since the character was first introduced

00:02:12.120 --> 00:02:15.920
in Lin's 2002 crime drama feature debut Better
Luck Tomorrow.

00:02:16.209 --> 00:02:21.040
Actor Sung Kang revealed in a 2013 interview
with Mandatory that Han was added to the Fast

00:02:21.040 --> 00:02:26.180
and Furious franchise only after Lin convinced
executives to change up another proposed character.

00:02:26.180 --> 00:02:30.500
Clearly, Han is not only beloved by the Fast
fandom, but he's also a character Lin has

00:02:30.500 --> 00:02:32.160
carried with him through his career.

00:02:32.500 --> 00:02:36.660
Han is a prime example of the narrative the
Fast and Furious saga has built around found

00:02:36.660 --> 00:02:39.700
family, and that may be important going into
the next film.

00:02:39.840 --> 00:02:42.560
Lin is certainly not treating the character's
return lightly.

00:02:42.690 --> 00:02:43.900
He told Entertainment Weekly:

00:02:43.900 --> 00:02:46.670
"In this world, I feel like things happen
for a reason.

00:02:46.670 --> 00:02:50.209
I won't go into details or anything, but I
do think that bringing him back is nothing

00:02:50.209 --> 00:02:54.709
I take lightly - and it took a lot - but I
think what I appreciate is that this universe

00:02:54.709 --> 00:02:59.000
has really grown and it allows us to evolve
and really kind of redefine ourselves as we

00:02:59.000 --> 00:02:59.500
go."

00:02:59.540 --> 00:03:00.860
As Han himself would say:

00:03:01.600 --> 00:03:02.680
"Life's simple.

00:03:03.960 --> 00:03:05.880
You make choices, and you don't look back."

00:03:06.240 --> 00:03:10.600
As for Sung Kang, the experience of returning
to the screen as the fan-favorite is as big

00:03:10.610 --> 00:03:14.040
for him as it is for the fans who have desperately
wanted to see him back.

00:03:14.040 --> 00:03:15.490
He told the Los Angeles Times:

00:03:15.490 --> 00:03:19.090
"It's emotional - it feels like I'm going
back to a family reunion.

00:03:19.090 --> 00:03:22.560
It's a relationship that has been missing
in my life since the last Fast."

00:03:22.780 --> 00:03:27.640
See Han Lue make his long-awaited return when
F9 drives into theaters on May 22.

